        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Court Cases: Lochner v. New York; Cooley v. Board of Wardens\n- Organizations: U.S. Supreme Court\n- Concepts: Fourteenth Amendment; Commerce Clause; labor law\n\nFacts:\n- In 1852, Cooley v. Board of Wardens, 53 U.S. 299, was a United States Supreme Court case.\n- In Cooley v. Board of Wardens, the U.S. Supreme Court held that a Pennsylvania law requiring ships entering or leaving Philadelphia to hire a local pilot did not violate the Commerce Clause of the Constitution.\n- In 1905, Lochner v. New York, 198 U.S. 45, was a landmark U.S. labor law case in the U.S. Supreme Court.\n- In Lochner v. New York, the U.S. Supreme Court held that limits on working time violated the Fourteenth Amendment.",
